{% comment %}
  The sticky search panel, replacing snippets/dT_top-search.liquid.

  The original was a Vue template -- v-model, v-for, :class -- rendered by
  assets/dT_main.js, a 125 KB webpack bundle of Vue plus axios, with
  dT_main_app.js on top. Two libraries and 148 KB to autocomplete a search box.
  This is plain markup driven by assets/suf-search.js, which calls Shopify's
  native /search/suggest.json.

  The legacy snippet is untouched; the legacy header still renders it.

  Accessibility: this is a combobox. The input owns the listbox via
  aria-controls, reports open state with aria-expanded, and points at the
  highlighted option with aria-activedescendant. Results are announced through
  the status region rather than silently appearing. suf-search.js maintains all
  of it -- if you change the markup, keep those attributes in sync.

  It degrades correctly with no JavaScript: the form is a real GET to
  routes.search_url, so pressing Enter searches. Only the suggestions are lost.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  /search/suggest.json returns price as a bare number, so the symbol has to
  come from Liquid rather than be hardcoded in the module.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="suf-search" data-suf-search data-currency-symbol="{{ cart.currency.symbol }}" hidden>
  <div class="suf-search__inner">
    <form
      class="suf-search__form"
      method="get"
      action="{{ routes.search_url }}"
      role="search"
      autocomplete="off"
    >
      <label class="suf-search__label" for="suf-search-input">
        {{ 'general.search.placeholder' | t | default: 'Search' }}
      </label>

      <div class="suf-search__field">
        <input
          type="search"
          id="suf-search-input"
          name="q"
          class="suf-search__input"
          placeholder="{{ 'general.search.placeholder' | t | default: 'Search our store' }}"
          autocomplete="off"
          role="combobox"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="suf-search-results"
          aria-autocomplete="list"
        >
        <input type="hidden" name="options[prefix]" value="last">

        <button class="suf-search__submit" type="submit">
          {% render 'suf-icon', icon: 'search', label: 'Search' %}
        </button>
      </div>

      <button class="suf-search__close" type="button" data-suf-search-close aria-label="Close search">
        {% render 'suf-icon', icon: 'close' %}
      </button>
    </form>

    <ul
      class="suf-search__results"
      id="suf-search-results"
      role="listbox"
      aria-label="Search suggestions"
      hidden
    ></ul>

    <p class="suf-search__status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>
</div>
